   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the assessors of the town of Whitestown and the village of New York Mills to accept an application for real property tax exemption from New York Mills Historical Society for certain parcels of land in such village and town",
    "basePrintNo": "S5434",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5434-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5434\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize the assessors of the\ntown of Whitestown and the village of New York Mills\nto accept an\napplication for real property tax exemption from New York Mills\nHistorical Society for certain parcels of land in\nsuch village and town\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis bill would allow assessors of the Town of Whitestown and Village\nof New York Mills to accept an application for a property tax\nexemption from the New York Mills Historical Society.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection one of the bill would authorize the assessors of the Town of\nWhitestown and the Village of New York Mills to accept an application\nfor real property tax exemption from the New York Mills Historical\nSociety for the parcel currently owned by this not-for-profit\nlocated at 96 Main Street in the Village of New York Mills for the\n2010 assessment rolls.\n\nSection two shall provide for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation has been requested by the New York Mills Historical\nSociety, a not-for-profit organization located in the Village of New\nYork Mills (Oneida county). The New York Mills Historical Society\nmoved its location to 96 Main Street in the Village of New York Mills\nin 2010, but did not acquire such property until after the taxable\nstatus date. Due to the timing of the acquisition, they were unable\nto apply and receive a real property tax exemption for the 2010\nassessment roll. This legislation will authorize the Village of New\nYork Mills and the Town of Whitestown to accept a retroactive\napplication for the 2010 tax year.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n\n",
